  "conclusions": [
    "Bare --env KEY removes inherited image value only when KEY is absent from Docker CLI process environment. KEY= remains a present empty value.",
    "Pinned Engine retains bare KEY markers in stored Config.Env; inspect returns that stored configuration.",
    "Pinned Engine removes markers when constructing OCI process environment. A Config.Env parser requiring '=' in every row would incorrectly reject the valid removal representation.",
    "Require exactly four authorized Android bare markers once each; reject unknown bare markers, duplicate keys and every Android KEY=value including empty.",
    "Compare all other configuration values exactly and derive effective environment by removing authorized markers. Keep SDK/UI absence guards.",
    "Keep clean explicit Docker CLI child environment and private empty Docker config; do not infer absence of SDK files from environment removal."
  ],
